// A boundary fixture — see BOUNDARY.txt, the number
// boundary. A tiny fraction: one significant digit at
// a deep scale. Swift reads the literal below as
// 5e-29; the Nifla-written reader reads
// 4.9999999999999993e-29, one ulp lower — so the
// token dump, the tree dump and the generated Swift
// disagree on the number, while the check verdict
// agrees (both sides accept: no verdict reads a
// value that finely).
let x = 0.00000000000000000000000000005
say x
